Because $10 \div \blue{4} = \green{2}
\text{ remainder } \red{2}$ ,
$
\qquad \begin{eqnarray}
i ^ {10} &=& (i^\blue{4})^\green{2}
\cdot i^\red{2} \\
&=& (1)^\green{2}
